# Git attributes.
#
# Purpose: keep the language bar on the repository page honest.
#
# driver/sysvad/ is the Microsoft Windows-driver-samples sysvad virtual audio
# driver sample (MS-PL, see driver/SYSVAD-LICENSE.txt and NOTICE). It is about
# 425k lines across 276 files and it is vendored, not written here. Without
# this file GitHub counts it as project code, and the language bar reads as if
# this repository were a large multi-language driver project instead of a small
# C++ engine plus one HTML page.
#
# driver/toolset-glue/ is likewise a build-time copy of Microsoft build glue,
# and tools/ carries prebuilt binaries (WebView2 SDK files, gh.exe).
#
# Marking a path linguist-vendored excludes it from the language bar and from
# the statistics. The files stay in the repository, stay searchable, and stay
# covered by their own licenses.

driver/** linguist-vendored
tools/** linguist-vendored
.github/** linguist-documentation

# Markdown files are documentation, not code.
*.md linguist-documentation
docs/** linguist-documentation

# No "text eol=" rules on purpose: they would rewrite every source file in the
# repository on the next commit, which is a large diff for no gain.
